-- ============================================================================
-- DR12 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Well Cost & Time, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE TIME. A rig is rented by the day, so a schedule is
-- a cost estimate wearing different units, and this tier reads the schedule
-- before anybody has priced anything.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON, AND IT IS THE SAME ONE THE ENGINE'S OWN
-- HEADER FELL INTO. The non-productive allowance is a STRETCH on productive
-- time: a fraction f gives nptHr = f * productiveHr exactly, so as a share of
-- ELAPSED time it is f/(1+f) and always smaller. The 12.5 percent allowance on
-- the published well is 11.11 percent of elapsed. A planner wanting a fifth of
-- the schedule non-productive enters 0.20 and gets 16.7 percent, and at f =
-- 0.5 someone reading f as the elapsed share plans 32 days against a real 24.
-- Two invariants make it checkable: productive hours never move as f changes,
-- and every activity keeps its share of the total under the stretch.
--
-- THREE CLOSED FORMS WITH THREE DIFFERENT SHAPES. Drilling is a HYPERBOLA in
-- rate, so rate times hours is invariant at fixed interval and a third of the
-- rate triples the hours. A round trip is EXACTLY twice the one way at every
-- depth, no exceptions. Running casing is AFFINE, one leg plus a flat term
-- that no running speed can touch: at an absurd 5,000 metres an hour a 2,000 m
-- run still takes 19.4 hours against a 19 hour floor. Three shapes, three
-- different things a designer can do about them.
--
-- AND THE BIT IS RARELY TURNING. On the capstone well it is on bottom for 40.4
-- percent of elapsed time. That number surprises people, and it is the reason
-- the productive and non-productive split earns its keep: the two have
-- different remedies, one bought back with rate and planning and the other
-- with risk management.
--
-- An activity in this tier carries NO cost. Money arrives in the next tier,
-- and the only two numbers that travel there are total days and drilled metres.
-- ============================================================================

values ('wellcost', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-this-course-decides","title":"What This Course Decides","lesson_keys":["l01-time-is-the-cost","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-two-currencies"]},{"key":"m02-the-activity","title":"The Activity","lesson_keys":["l01-a-programme-is-a-list-of-activities","l02-the-four-kinds","l03-what-each-kind-needs","l04-the-flat-activity","l05-what-an-activity-does-not-carry"]},{"key":"m03-the-closed-forms","title":"The Closed Forms","lesson_keys":["l01-drilling-is-interval-over-rate","l02-tripping-is-twice-the-depth","l03-running-casing-is-both","l04-why-closed-forms-at-all","l05-what-the-forms-leave-out"]},{"key":"m04-productive-and-non-productive","title":"Productive and Non-Productive","lesson_keys":["l01-the-split","l02-what-counts-as-npt","l03-trouble-time-and-the-allowance","l04-the-bit-is-rarely-turning","l05-why-the-distinction-earns-its-keep"]},{"key":"m05-rolling-up-a-programme","title":"Rolling Up a Programme","lesson_keys":["l01-hours-into-days","l02-drilled-metres","l03-reading-a-schedule","l04-the-numbers-that-travel"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
